        '3-5', $q$Our Moon$q$, $q$(1) The Moon is Earth's closest neighbor in space. (2) It travels all the way around Earth about once a month. (3) The Moon does not make its own light. (4) We can see it because sunlight shines on it.

(5) The Moon seems to change shape during the month. (6) These different shapes are called phases. (7) A full moon looks like a bright, round circle. (8) A new moon is very hard to see in the night sky.

(9) The Moon has no air to breathe. (10) It has no wind or rain, either. (11) In 1969, astronauts walked on the Moon for the first time. (12) They left footprints in the dusty ground. (13) ___ there is no wind to blow the dust away, many of those footprints are likely still there. (14) I want to be an astronaut someday.$q$, 'draft')
