   $q$Which sentence uses a progressive verb tense correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Yesterday, the baby is crying all morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"present-with-past-signal"},{"text":"Tomorrow, we were painting the fence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"past-with-future-signal"},{"text":"Right now, the team was warming up on the field.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"past-with-present-signal"},{"text":"Next summer, Grandma will be teaching me to knit.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Next summer, Grandma will be teaching me to knit.$q$, $q$"Next summer" points to the future, and "will be teaching" is the future progressive, so the time and the verb match. "Right now" needs the present "is warming up," not the past "was warming up."$q$, 'draft', null)
